<title>SOUTH AFRICA: FORECAST - S.African economic indicators consensus.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - S.African economic indicators consensus.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African economic indicators scheduled for release next week include:</p>
<p>DAY----GMT---INDICATOR----PERIOD--FORECAST---RANGE-----PREVIOUS</p>
<p>WED    0900  CPI Y/Y	MAY     9.8 PCT    9.6/10.1  9.9</p>
<p>WED    0900  CPI M/M	MAY     0.6	  0.4/0.9   0.9</p>
<p>WED+   1000  TRADE	  MAY     +0.85 BLN +0.5/1.1   +0.73</p>
<p>FRI    1500  M3 Y/Y	 MAY     15.19 PCT 14.2/16.35 15.44</p>
<p>FRI    1500  PVT CREDIT   MAY     16.56 PCT 16.0/16.82 16.95</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Individual forecasts:</p>
<p>			  CPI Y/Y    M3	    CREDIT     TRADE</p>
<p>			  (pct)	(pct)	 (pct)	(bln rand)</p>
<p>Boland Bank	    9.8	 16.25	 16.8	 n/a</p>
<p>BOE NatWest	    9.8	 15.00	 16.00	+0.9</p>
<p>Edey Rogers	    9.7	 14.4	  16.8	 n/a</p>
<p>Equisec		  9.8	 14.2	  16.5	 +0.8</p>
<p>Huysamer Stals	10.1	 16.35	 16.82	+0.5</p>
<p>JP Morgan		9.6	 15.7	  16.6	 +1.1</p>
<p>Mathison &amp; Hollidge  9.8	 14.6	  16.8	 +0.85</p>
<p>Nedcor		   9.7	 15.1	  16.1	 +1.0</p>
<p>Rand Merchant Bank   9.9	 15.7/16.3   16.4/16.8  +0.7/1.0</p>
<p>Unattributable	 9.8	 14.45	 16.6	 +0.9</p>
<p>Unattributable	10.0	 15.09	 16.5	 n/a</p>
<p>NOTE: Economists said their forecasts for the trade balance were only an indication as the figure was difficult to forecast. The data is volatile due to the inclusion of trade statistics from Botswana, Lesotho, Namibia and Swaziland.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
